BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Noir: Kansas City (1996)
DTSTART:20260220T014500Z
DTEND:20260220T041000Z
DTSTAMP:20260220T014500Z
UID:BtxkcMDG6T
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 128 mins (2h08m)\n\nJennifer Jason Leigh plays a Jea
 n Harlow-obsessed housewife who abducts the spouse of a local politician b
 efore the 1934 Democratic primary election. She goes on a wild ride\, and 
 so will you courtesy of Altman’s spirited recreations of the 1930s jazz 
 scene.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/programs-and-events/noir-city/kansas-city\n
 \nEstimated start: 18:00
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Downtown\, 2100 4th Avenue
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:D'Est (From the East) (1993)
DTSTART:20260220T030000Z
DTEND:20260220T052000Z
DTSTAMP:20260220T030000Z
UID:ta5TfLRH0B
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 125 mins (2h05m)\n\nPresented by Mount Analogue ◦
  Art + Cinema with Seattle Documentary Association From director Chantal 
 Akerman (Jeanne Dielman)\, D’Est (From the East) retraces a journey from
  the end of summer to deepest winter\, from East Germany\, across Poland a
 nd Ukraine\, to Moscow. It is a voyage Akerman wanted to make shortly afte
 r the collapse of the Soviet bloc "before it was too late\," reconstructin
 g her impressions in the manner of a documentary on the border of fiction.
 By filming "everything that touched me\," Akerman sifts through and fixes 
 upon sounds and images as she follows the thread of this subjective crossi
 ng. Without dialogue or commentary\, From the East is a cinematographic el
 egy.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/cinema/in-theaters/dest-(from-the-east)\n\nEs
 timated start: 19:15
